{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"weedy-distant-asp","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe MCP `review_plan` tool (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`) derives whether it signs a plan-review\nattestation SOLELY from server read-only mode: it calls the library with\n`sign=not ro, emit_sidecar=not ro`. There is no caller-facing `sign` parameter, so an MCP\nclient cannot request an explicit unsigned review the way a CLI caller can with `--no-sign`\nor a library caller can with `sign=False`. Conversely, when read-only mode DOES suppress\nsigning, the returned verdict carries no machine-readable reason saying so — a client sees an\nunsigned PASS and cannot distinguish \"policy suppressed the signature\" from \"signing failed\".\n\nSplit out of epic 58f2-b6ed-363e-4608 (uninformed-aspiring-rhino) on 2026-07-24: the CLI and\nlibrary boundaries of that epic are a test/help-hardening job, while this is a genuine public\nAPI change to a different boundary with tool-schema and generated-reference consequences.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n- MCP `review_plan` accepts `sign: bool = True`, matching the library default.\n- An explicit `sign=False` runs the review without signing, and the result names the caller's\n  opt-out as the unsigned reason.\n- Read-only server mode continues to suppress signing regardless of the requested value, and\n  the result carries a machine-readable unsigned reason identifying the read-only policy\n  (distinct from the caller-opt-out reason and from a signing failure).\n- The tool docstring states the sign-by-default contract and both unsigned exceptions.\n\n## Approach\n1. Add `sign: bool = True` to the MCP `review_plan` signature; pass `sign=sign and not ro`.\n2. Introduce a machine-readable unsigned-reason field on the verdict distinguishing:\n   `caller-opt-out`, `readonly-policy`, `not-signable` (BLOCK/INDETERMINATE/degraded/local),\n   and `sign-failed`. Reuse the existing `signature.signed` boolean as the primary contract;\n   the reason is additive, so existing consumers stay byte-compatible.\n3. Update the tool docstring and regenerate `docs/mcp-reference.md`.\n\nRejected: inferring the reason client-side from the verdict shape — the read-only and\nnot-signable cases are indistinguishable without server knowledge, which is the bug.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py` (unsigned-reason plumbing, if the reason is\n  produced at the finalization seam rather than the MCP boundary)\n- MCP surface tests for plan review\n- `docs/mcp-reference.md` (generated tool inventory / outputSchema)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] MCP `review_plan` exposes `sign: bool = True`; a contract test proves the default\n      persists an attestation and `sign=False` does not.\n- [ ] With `sign=False`, the result carries a machine-readable unsigned reason identifying the\n      caller opt-out; a test asserts the exact reason value.\n- [ ] In read-only mode the result is unsigned regardless of the requested `sign` value and\n      carries the read-only-policy reason, distinct from the caller-opt-out reason; a\n      table-driven test covers (sign x readonly) combinations.\n- [ ] A never-signable verdict (BLOCK / INDETERMINATE / degraded / local source) reports the\n      not-signable reason rather than the opt-out or read-only reason.\n- [ ] The MCP tool docstring states sign-by-default and names both unsigned exceptions;\n      `docs/mcp-reference.md` regenerates cleanly and matches.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the default non-integration pytest suite exit zero.\n","id":"2cd3-062b-f99d-4143","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"MCP review_plan has no caller-facing sign opt-out and no machine-readable unsigned reason"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1784935536323295001,"uuid":"74532fdb-b8c6-40a9-b1b9-3333a151cfee"}